-- title:
--   Igusa components of the descended two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a level $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$. Let $W$ be the finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ that are supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base-changed field of modular functions along $A$ whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series over $A$ ($hR_0$). Further data: $\pi \in A \cap K_0$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; families $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$ ($\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$) and $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ ($s \in W$) of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, subject to: $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line $[1:0]$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction; each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$ is the pullback of that one under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\bar\gamma \cdot [1:0] = \ell$; $\ell \mapsto \mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$ is injective and the family is permuted by all such pullbacks; each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss},s}$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in exactly $A$, is fixed by all those pullbacks, contains the image of every $R_0$-integral $f$ that is regular wherever $j$ is and whose reduction is $s$-integral (with $f - a$ in the maximal ideal whenever $\mathrm{residue}\,a$ matches the $s$-value of the reduction), and contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for all $a \in A$. Descent data: a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with a local injection $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, with surjective induced residue map, with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$; the subfield $F_0 \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, which contains the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$ and carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $\iota$; and $S$ equal to $\{\hat\jmath\}$ or $\{\hat\jmath^{-1}\}$. Then there is a map $\ell \mapsto \mathfrak q_\ell$ from $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ to ideals of $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg}\,A_0\,F_0\,S$ (the elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[S]$) such that: for every $\ell$ and $x \in F_0$, the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$ if and only if $x = b/c$ with $b, c$ in the chart algebra and $c \notin \mathfrak q_\ell$; each $\mathfrak q_\ell$ is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; $\ell \mapsto \mathfrak q_\ell$ is injective; and every minimal prime over that ideal is some $\mathfrak q_\ell$.
--
--   This identifies the irreducible components of the special fibre of the descended two-chart integral model over the small base $A_0$ with the $q+1$ Igusa components indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$: the components are pairwise distinct, exhaust the minimal primes over the uniformiser, and the localisation at the component $\ell$ is the trace on $F_0$ of the Igusa valuation ring $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig},\ell}$. It feeds the subsequent analysis of maximal ideals of the chart algebras and of the Drinfeld (supersingular) rings along the descended model.
